  "result": "`split_arg_string` now keeps `#` as an ordinary character, so `split_arg_string(\"cmd a#b\")` returns `[\"cmd\", \"a#b\"]`. `python -m pytest tests/test_shell_completion.py -q` passes (59 tests).\n\nThe fix is one line in `src/click/shell_completion.py`: `lex.commenters = \"\"` after the other lexer settings. I added `test_split_arg_string_hash_is_not_comment` at the end of `tests/test_shell_completion.py`. It also checks that a token starting with `#`, as in `\"cmd #b\"`, comes back as `\"#b\"`.\n\nI only ran the one test file, not the full suite. I didn't confirm that the new test fails without the fix.",
